{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-minecraft/audio/main-9b14f9cde45a.mp3","durationSec":288.696,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":1.96,"text":"Most video games give you a clear goal."},{"start":2.6,"end":4.68,"text":"In a racing game, you must win the race."},{"start":5.52,"end":6.42,"text":"Minecraft is different."},{"start":7.12,"end":8.34,"text":"Nobody tells you what to do."},{"start":8.82,"end":11.7,"text":"You can build a house, explore a valley, or just walk around."},{"start":12.72,"end":14.02,"text":"Minecraft gives players freedom."},{"start":14.74,"end":16.5,"text":"There are no goals that you must reach."},{"start":17,"end":18.16,"text":"You choose how to play."},{"start":18.94,"end":21.3,"text":"Some players build big structures from blocks."},{"start":22.3,"end":23.32,"text":"Others explore the world."},{"start":24.18,"end":28.7,"text":"Some players craft things, which means they make new items from simple materials."},{"start":29.36,"end":32.38,"text":"In survival play, you must also stay alive."},{"start":33.32,"end":35.98,"text":"In creative play, you can simply build what you want."},{"start":36.9,"end":38.54,"text":"This is like a box of toy bricks."},{"start":39.26,"end":41.06,"text":"The box does not tell you what to make."},{"start":41.5,"end":43.16,"text":"The bricks only give you the pieces."},{"start":44.24,"end":47.34,"text":"In the same way, Minecraft gives you a world and lets you choose."},{"start":48.06,"end":49.86,"text":"So the game is not one activity."},{"start":50.34,"end":53.02,"text":"It is many possible activities in one place."},{"start":53.76,"end":56.36,"text":"Many people think a big company planned Minecraft."},{"start":56.36,"end":58.8,"text":"In fact, it began with one man."},{"start":58.8,"end":63.88,"text":"Markus Persson created the first Minecraft, and he wrote it in Java, a computer language."},{"start":63.88,"end":66.14,"text":"Persson did not start from nothing."},{"start":66.72,"end":70.2,"text":"In April 2009, another game called Infiniminer came out."},{"start":70.8,"end":75.22,"text":"It gave Persson ideas for his own early project, called RubyDung."},{"start":75.22,"end":81.04,"text":"Infiniminer influenced three important things: the blocky look, the first-person view, and the building with blocks."},{"start":81.8,"end":84.88,"text":"In a first-person view, you see the world through the eyes of your character."},{"start":85.64,"end":88.04,"text":"The exact early dates are not completely certain."},{"start":88.78,"end":93.98,"text":"But the usual story is this: in May 2009, the game began as Cave Game."},{"start":94.64,"end":97.72,"text":"In December 2009, it entered a stage called Indev."},{"start":98.82,"end":102.52,"text":"Then, in June 2010, it entered the Alpha stage."},{"start":103.54,"end":106.08,"text":"So Minecraft did not appear as a finished product."},{"start":106.6,"end":108.12,"text":"It began as an experiment."},{"start":108.68,"end":112.68,"text":"It borrowed good ideas from another game and slowly became something new."},{"start":113.22,"end":115.84,"text":"Minecraft grew step by step, in public."},{"start":116.64,"end":121.32,"text":"Each stage, from Cave Game to Indev to Alpha, was a new and better version."},{"start":122.12,"end":125.32,"text":"Then, in 2011, the full game came out."},{"start":125.92,"end":128.96,"text":"After the full release, something important changed."},{"start":129.92,"end":134.18,"text":"On 1 December 2011, Persson stepped down as lead developer."},{"start":134.76,"end":136.8,"text":"He gave control to Jens Bergensten."},{"start":137.48,"end":140.32,"text":"This means the game did not depend on its creator anymore."},{"start":140.68,"end":142.76,"text":"A team could now carry it forward."},{"start":143.46,"end":145.18,"text":"The game kept growing after that."},{"start":146.14,"end":149.74,"text":"In 2012, adventure mode and command blocks arrived."},{"start":150.48,"end":156.74,"text":"With these tools, players could create their own maps with their own rules and challenges, and share them with others."},{"start":157.58,"end":159.72,"text":"So players were not only playing the game."},{"start":160.28,"end":162.86,"text":"They were also making new games inside it."},{"start":163.6,"end":164.26,"text":"This matters."},{"start":164.78,"end":168.86,"text":"A game that only one person controls can stop when that person leaves."},{"start":169.68,"end":175.22,"text":"Minecraft moved from one creator to a team, and also gave players tools to create."},{"start":175.82,"end":177.4,"text":"That helped it keep changing."},{"start":178.48,"end":181.96,"text":"Now we come back to the common idea that Microsoft made Minecraft."},{"start":182.82,"end":183.44,"text":"It did not."},{"start":184.38,"end":186.58,"text":"Microsoft bought Minecraft much later."},{"start":187.28,"end":191.26,"text":"In November 2014, Microsoft bought Mojang, the company behind the game."},{"start":191.96,"end":195.5,"text":"It also bought the rights to Minecraft as an idea and a product."},{"start":196.06,"end":199.18,"text":"The price was 2.5 billion US dollars."},{"start":199.18,"end":200.7,"text":"Look at the timeline."},{"start":200.7,"end":203.74,"text":"Persson started the game in 2009."},{"start":204.62,"end":206.62,"text":"The full game came out in 2011."},{"start":207.88,"end":209.16,"text":"Microsoft bought it in 2014."},{"start":210.34,"end":212.74,"text":"So Microsoft did not create the success."},{"start":213.52,"end":216.2,"text":"It paid for a game that was already successful."},{"start":217.12,"end":219.46,"text":"That is why the price was so high."},{"start":220.04,"end":223.16,"text":"A company does not pay billions for an untested idea."},{"start":223.16,"end":226.32,"text":"It pays for something that people already love."},{"start":226.32,"end":229.98,"text":"Minecraft has sold over 400 million copies."},{"start":230.74,"end":233.14,"text":"It is the best-selling video game ever."},{"start":233.9,"end":238.76,"text":"Even before the full release in 2011, it had sold more than four million copies."},{"start":239.5,"end":241.28,"text":"The harder question is why."},{"start":242.08,"end":244.54,"text":"Some things certainly helped the game become famous."},{"start":245.06,"end":246.48,"text":"People shared it on social media."},{"start":246.48,"end":248.68,"text":"Fans made funny copies of it."},{"start":249.08,"end":253.84,"text":"There were other versions of the game, products to buy, and fan meetings called Minecon."},{"start":254.52,"end":256.36,"text":"All of these spread the name of the game."},{"start":257.04,"end":257.86,"text":"But be careful here."},{"start":258.38,"end":261.46,"text":"Many people say Minecraft sold so well because of its freedom."},{"start":261.98,"end":268.38,"text":"That is a reasonable idea, because the game has no required goals and lets you build, explore and survive."},{"start":269.1,"end":270.66,"text":"But nobody has proved it."},{"start":271.06,"end":273.26,"text":"It is one possible explanation."},{"start":274.2,"end":276.04,"text":"So we need to separate two things."},{"start":276.56,"end":279.46,"text":"We know the sales number, because people counted the copies."},{"start":280.06,"end":282.78,"text":"We do not know all the reasons for the sales."},{"start":283.52,"end":288.04,"text":"When someone gives a reason, we should ask: can they show it, or are they guessing?"}],"words":[{"text":"Most","start":0,"end":0.28},{"text":"video","start":0.28,"end":0.52},{"text":"games","start":0.52,"end":0.86},{"text":"give","start":0.86,"end":1.04},{"text":"you","start":1.04,"end":1.18},{"text":"a","start":1.18,"end":1.3},{"text":"clear","start":1.3,"end":1.58},{"text":"goal","start":1.58,"end":1.96},{"text":"In","start":2.6,"end":2.7},{"text":"a","start":2.7,"end":2.82},{"text":"racing","start":2.82,"end":3.04},{"text":"game","start":3.04,"end":3.44},{"text":"you","start":3.66,"end":3.68},{"text":"must","st